# =====================================================================
# rb4011_dns_resolver_delta — HD-317: TECHNETIUM DNS-PRIMARY ON ROUTER (DHCP + /ip dns)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Transient delta (network-ops.md 3-tier): sets the DHCP dns-server chain per VLAN —
# VPS PRIMARY -> oldsrv SECONDARY -> Pi TERTIARY by default, HOME-FIRST (Pi -> VPS ->
# oldsrv) on every VLAN whose `network_vlans` row carries `lan_first_dns: true`.
# RouterOS /ip dhcp-server network accepts AT MOST 3 dns-server values (a 4th is silently
# dropped; the earlier 4-entry rendition dropped Pi), so the router /ip dns is NOT part of
# the DHCP list. The router's own /ip dns upstream (below) is the implicit
# final fallback: clients that can't reach any of the 3 resolvers still have the
# router-resolver as their gateway.
# ⚠ The ORDER is not cosmetic: the three instances answer the home-hosted app names with
# DIFFERENT addresses (per-instance split-horizon, docs/network-dns.md §Per-Instance
# Split-Horizon), so whichever instance a VLAN queries first decides whether that VLAN sees
# the home edge or the VPS edge. HD-1095 (2026-10-07) put VLAN 50 (Media) home-first for
# exactly that reason: with the VPS first the Shield got media.kogler.si = dns_primary_ip
# and the VPS edge answered 404 for the home-hosted names — those VPS-edge routes landed the same
# evening, so this chain is resilience (home-first keeps the Media VLAN working if WAN or the VPS
# resolver is down), not the thing that makes media resolve.
# Final state is ALSO folded into rb4011_converge.rsc.j2 (its idempotency is
# partial by design — /add dupes abort re-imports before the DNS section) and into
# roles/router/tasks/main.yml — all three read the same `lan_first_dns` SSOT.
# Render: playbooks/render-converge.yml; apply: scripts/routeros-apply-delta.sh.
# =====================================================================
# DHCP — per-VLAN resolver chain (3 max), rendered from the `network_vlans` SSOT
{% for v in network_vlans %}
/ip dhcp-server network set [find where address={{ v.subnet }}] dns-server={{ ([dns_tertiary_ip, dns_primary_ip, dns_secondary_ip] if (v.lan_first_dns | default(false)) else [dns_primary_ip, dns_secondary_ip, dns_tertiary_ip]) | join(',') }}
{% endfor %}
# Router resolver upstream — VPS,oldsrv,Pi + Cloudflare last (final unfiltered resort)
/ip dns set allow-remote-requests=yes servers={{ dns_primary_ip }},{{ dns_secondary_ip }},{{ dns_tertiary_ip }},1.1.1.1,1.0.0.1
# =====================================================================